WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.525
Unit 1 is the order.

2
00:00:01.525 --> 00:00:06.329
The guide's steps are numbered to match
the twelve network topics of the Zero Trust

3
00:00:06.329 --> 00:00:10.144
closure update, but they run in a
different order, so the logs exist

4
00:00:10.144 --> 00:00:14.312
before anything is enforced, and
nothing blocks before its path exists.

5
00:00:14.312 --> 00:00:18.137
First the decision, the architecture,
and Step twelve's logging.

6
00:00:18.137 --> 00:00:23.350
Then the client, Microsoft traffic, the
compliant network, and tenant restrictions.

7
00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:26.853
Then private applications,
privileged protocols,

8
00:00:26.853 --> 00:00:29.438
internet traffic, and T L S inspection.

9
00:00:29.438 --> 00:00:35.000
Last, coexistence and migration, and Step
twelve again, for the evidence package.

10
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.712
This path follows that order.

11
00:00:36.712 --> 00:00:42.287
One more rule: Microsoft's network access
A P I's are on the Graph beta endpoint.

12
00:00:42.287 --> 00:00:45.073
Learn says beta A P I's
are subject to change

13
00:00:45.073 --> 00:00:48.176
and not supported in
production applications.

14
00:00:48.176 --> 00:00:51.042
So the guide runs
Learn's requests by hand,

15
00:00:51.042 --> 00:00:54.837
as an administrator, and
keeps each result as evidence.

16
00:00:54.837 --> 00:00:57.910
Every lab uses the
guide's placeholder table.
